# The credentials of the stack of the agent of PACA.
#
# This file is the manifest of the stack: the installer of the environment
# reads it, offers every value with its default and writes the `.env` next
# to it. The manual fallback still works:
#
#   cp hermes/env.example hermes/.env
#
# The metadata of the manifest lives in the comments of the file, so it
# stays a valid Compose `env_file` and there is no second file to keep in
# sync. The directives of a key are:
#
#   # @secret     the value is a secret: it is never printed and the file
#                that holds it is written with the mode 600
#   # @generate   a strong value can be generated for the key
#   # @required   the stack cannot run without the value: the installer
#                refuses to finish the interactive run without it
#
# Any other comment line directly above a key is its description: the text
# the person who installs reads.

# The key of the provider of the models. The agent calls OpenRouter with
# it, and it is the only credential the agent cannot work without: the
# stack refuses to come up when it is missing.
#
# The value belongs to the DevOps engineer who runs the project: the
# installer asks for it and writes it to `hermes/.env`, and nobody reads
# that file.
# @secret
# @required
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# The model of the agent: the id of the model on the provider. The default
# is the one the project starts with.
AGENT_MAIN_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash
